# Adaptive review gate

After code-changing work and ordinary verification, decide whether a review-fix loop is needed. Do not start the loop for read-only answers, docs-only edits, or when the user explicitly skipped review.

## Immediate review

Start `adaptive-code-review-loop` immediately if any of the following is involved:

- security / auth
- migrations / data mutation
- concurrency
- public API / contracts
- deployment

## Score

+1 for each item. Threshold **>= 3** — start `adaptive-code-review-loop`. Below that, finish without the loop and say in one line that the gate skipped review.

- more than 3 production files
- more than 150 non-generated diff lines
- several modules / services
- a new dependency / config
- substantial behavioral edge cases
- multi-layer testing

Explicit `/adaptive-code-review-loop` bypasses the gate. So does delegated invocation — a required stage of another process or skill.

Procedure and stop rules live only in the skill. Do not fix an only-Minor round. Do not attach an always-on hook.
